
// IF with an OR condition
// Max Score: 2 | Difficulty: Not Specified
// Sometimes, you may want to perform a block of code if either of two conditions are true. Then you can use an OR condition.

// Write a program based on the following structured English:

// INPUT a boolean flag
// INPUT a string
// CHECK the length of the string and the state of the flag
// IF the string is longer than 6 characters OR the flag is true, ADD " WooHoo" to the back of the string
// IF not, ADD " Bummer" to the end of the string
// OUTPUT the string
// The expected input is:
// A boolean
// A string
// e.g. false
// "Beach"
// The expected output is:
// "Beach Bummer"

DECLARE flag : BOOLEAN
DECLARE str : STRING
INPUT flag
INPUT str
IF LENGTH(str)>6 OR flag=TRUE THEN
    OUTPUT str, " WooHoo"
    ELSE
    OUTPUT str," Bummer"  
ENDIF 